# The `+` menu's New ▸ child: the pointer opens it on row 0 (un-highlighted,
# as Rust's child starts), two downs land on the THIRD row and Enter runs it —
# the HTTP request opens; `→` on the child's row changes nothing (Rust's Right
# reads the parent's row). The first arrow used to only light the cursor, so
# every later key was one row above where the screen said it was, and `→`
# opened the curation list so Enter pinned instead of creating (walkthrough 2.2).
click 33 1
expect screen contains "Create…"
hover 36 3
expect screen contains "Scratch buffer"
key down
key down
key right
expect screen contains "HTTP request"
expect screen lacks "Pin to top"
key enter
expect screen lacks "Create…"
expect screen contains "new request"
